@startuml control-studio
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam linetype ortho

title truST Control Studio: Identify → Tune → Validate

package "VS Code webview" {
  component "Shared truST theme and controls\nimmediate checkbox dropdowns, compact editors, response charts" as shared_ui
  component "Identify\nplant inputs, measured outputs, method\nIdentify plant / Open recording / Limits\nmodel review: Identify plant / Reset study / Tune tab\nselected readings + response before identification\nmodel equation + applied input + measured/model response" as identify
  component "Tune\nactual controller instance or declared PID group\nmethod, Requirements, conditional Channels\nmanual/pinned settings + predicted response" as tune
  component "Validate\nmandatory results + measured response\nexplicit Apply / Restore previous settings" as validate
  component "Existing monitor projection\nbounded selected-signal history + current legend values\nscoped readings; gaps and restart boundaries" as readings
  component "Scoped host-state projection\noperation, binding and recovery state\npage navigation does not start work" as projection
  component "Contextual manual tools\nproject experiments, recorded fits, model analysis\nselected through existing methods\nshared model-comparison evidence and saved fit controls" as tools
  component "Loop setup form\nstructure: PID, cascade, feedforward, Smith predictor, gain schedule, PID group, ON/OFF,\nstate feedback, own P, PI or PID, other law\n(coefficients searched), or identify only\nprefilled from compiled calls; names the first missing item" as setup_form
}

package "VS Code extension host" {
  component "Panel message boundary\nproject, loop revision and editor session\ndeduplicated requests and current-scope checks" as panel
  component "Engine panel route (engine/enginePanelRoute.ts)\nstarts one trust-control-studio serve per window\na loop the engine serves: each page request goes to the engine\nin the order the page made it (study inputs first),\nand the engine's answers, updates and opened study go to the page\nno rule of its own; presentation and wiring only" as engine_route
  component "Compiled binding discovery\nexplicit configured loops, ST instances and PID group members\ncomplete signal/parameter/state mappings, compiled member checks" as bindings
  component "Loop setup generators\ncompiled catalog: symbols, call links, writes\none loop definition per structure\nwrites control-loops/<name>.json, never overwrites" as setup
  component "Automatic flow coordinator\nIdentify → model review\nexplicit Tune stops at candidate\nexplicit Validate checks model then controller\npause for missing inputs or failure" as flow
  component "TypeScript session (until V7)\nEngineer workflow session: request guards, input invalidation and recovery\none explicit session state: model, candidate, requirements and retained outcomes\nfor parked loops, and for what the engine does not serve yet:\nfits from an opened file, supplied models, analysis tools" as engineer
  component "Engineer action owners\nIdentify, Tune, Validate, Apply/confirm,\nRestore and runtime review; each works only\nthrough the session host and its state" as actions
  component "Study Reset\nidle/recovery guard; clear working results\npersist empty draft before refreshing view" as reset
  component "Model and recording owners\nopened or retained recordings\nindependent identification data and selected model" as models
  component "Automatic identification\nfresh applicable bounded acquisition\none live campaign + provisional model fit" as identification
  component "Project experiment and recording lifecycle\nreviewed activation, runtime scan buffers\nterminal restoration and retained raw signals" as experiments
  component "Existing analysis sessions\nselected model / declared controller\nroot locus, exact Routh, frequency and initial-state response\nminimal pole views, state structure and measured MIMO" as analysis
  component "Automatic test criteria\nmodel timescale, recording noise and operating limits\npreserve explicit values; freeze before validation" as automatic_criteria
  component "Controller adapters and tuning\nexisting Control.PID / declared project / state controllers\ncascade: inner first, outer through the closed inner loop\nfeedforward: PI on the output path, K_ff and lead/lag from both paths\nSmith predictor: model K, T, θ from the model; PI on the delay-free model\ndecoupler: D = K⁻¹·diag(K), each PI through it\nAutomatic: response chosen by its predicted requirements\nexplicit choices, parameter mapping and pins\nfinite Riccati stages with explicit fixed runtime policy" as tuning
  component "Independent model check\nfresh live recording; frozen model coefficients\nper-channel agreement and retained qualification\nfailed prediction retained; acceptance remains blocked" as model_check
  component "Verification campaign\nmandatory scenarios, initial states and constraints\nmissing scenarios remain Inconclusive" as campaign
  component "Selected-model simulation\nCurrent/Tuned prediction: Control.PID calculated,\nswitching, state-feedback, project laws and PID groups run as ST on the model\nexplicit model-envelope scenarios" as prediction
  component "Configured-plant validation\nCurrent/Tuned actual ST execution\nnominal campaign has no fitted-model override" as configured_validation
  component "Reviewed application coordinator\nfresh review and single confirmation\nexplicit Apply or Restore only" as application
  component "Commissioning and recovery\nwaits (bounded, cancellable) for the validated operating point\ncoherent parameters/state adoption; state-feedback entry allowance\nobserves the test in runtime time; monitoring and rollback" as commissioning
  database "TypeScript session study store\ncontrol-studio/[loop id]/typescript-session/study.json: draft, history,\npage, mimo sections; its own recordings/ and history/ folders,\nbeside the engine's study, never in its files (A8.3, §0.1a)\natomic writes in a later turn; refused over the loop's storage limit\nchecked results are shared, never checked again (A10.7)" as persistence
  database "VS Code workspace state\noperation journals only: identification campaign, recording\nowner, mode, commissioning checkpoints, experiment and apply\nrecovery, isolated-operation identity" as journals
  component "Identification campaign (identificationCampaign.ts)\nprocess time from recording samples; the wall clock only paces\nand supervises connection loss\n1. recording starts first  2. steady baseline (settleDetection.ts)\n3. one step per plant input, held until settled; a single step\nis finished early, pulses and relays run their duration\n4. restoration confirmed by the runtime before the next step" as ident_campaign
  component "Apply observation (applyObservation.ts)\nrecording starts before the validated target change;\nfollowed on process time; leaving the permitted range\nrestores the previous settings at once" as apply_obs
  component "Project loop definitions\ncontrol-loops/<name>.json, never overwritten" as loop_files
}

package "Rust engine: process trust-control-studio (checklist rust-logic-migration.md: V0 foundation, V1 Identify, V2 Tune, V3 Validate, V4 Apply/Restore/Keep, V5 setup; serves the panel from V6)" {
  component "trust-control-math (domain-neutral library)\nlinalg, model (transfer function, state space),\ndiscretize (exact ZOH, Tustin, Euler), simulate, sampling,\nidentify: low-order step-response fits, relay cycles, scoring\nfrequency, margins, SIMC/AMIGO/λ and the half rule, pole placement,\nclosed-loop simulation, polynomials, notch\nnumbers in, typed results out; no product knowledge" as rust_math
  component "trust-control (pure, no I/O)\nloop contract, signal reads (E3), recordings and their evidence (E4),\nexperiment plans and checks (E5), study container and sections,\nidentification rules: policy, campaign baseline and hold, review,\nmodel selection (N3.3), recorded limits (B3.4), provisional model;\ntuning rules: requirements, formulas, Automatic recommendation,\ndesign to requirements, candidates and pins, Control.PID prediction,\nmargins and robustness; study Tune section (A8.4);\nvalidation rules: plan, scenarios, campaign, run assessment (N8),\nmodel check, plant decision, isolated-run records; Validate section;\ncommissioning rules (B6, A6, C0, C1): starting point, Auto-entry allowance,\ntransfer records and checks (E6), parameter transactions (E7), initialization,\nobservation, the one Restore from the checkpoint, Keep's edits; Apply section;\nsetup rules (B1): compiled catalog, form model, generators, save;\nfailures with next actions (A11); json: every decode with normalized numbers" as rust_control
  component "trust-control-studio (engine crate and program)\nserve: JSON-RPC 2.0 on stdin/stdout, Content-Length frames\ncommand line (§0.1b): open, identify, tune, validate, apply, restore, keep, setup, cancel;\ntoken never an argument; apply/restore/keep: review, then --review <identity>\nmethods controlStudio/open | status | cancel | page | identify | tune | preview | validate |\napply | restore | keep | setupDiscover | setupSave\nIdentify workflow: campaign driver, reconciliation, recovery\nTune: Automatic, SIMC, AMIGO, relay rule, manual settings;\ndesigns from the study model, never writes to the controller;\nthe relay rule reads its recording; preview stores nothing\nValidate: live model check (provisional model), then isolated\nactual-ST runs of current and candidate per scenario (E8.4), journaled\nApply: starting point wait, Manual staging, parameters, Auto entry, observed\ntarget change; a failure after the first write runs the one Restore\nIdentify: enters and returns the mode its method needs (A6.2)\nlong operations: operationId at once, controlStudio/update" as rust_commands
  component "Runtime client (annex E1-E8) on trust-runtime-client\ncontrol endpoint client shared with trust-lsp inline values\nrequests checked before sending, answers before use\nrecording session; experiment start, status, finish, abort;\nisolated runs; transfers (E6) and parameter transactions (E7):\nowner retained before dispatch, a lost acknowledgement read by its identity" as rust_client
  database "Rust study files\ncontrol-studio/[loop id]/study.json + recordings/\nformat 1; earlier formats move to history/\nrecordings keep their evidence verdict" as rust_studies
  database "Operation journal (A8.3)\ntruST folder in the user's local state folder, one file per loop,\nshared by serve and the command line\nrecording owner, experiment and campaign\ncommissioning checkpoint, Identify mode change, isolated jobs\njournaled before dispatch; never a token" as rust_journal
}

package "Existing analysis and runtime services" {
  component "Bounded numerical workers\nidentification, tuning and model analysis" as workers
  component "Runtime connection/lifecycle owner\nexact simulator/project binding\nexisting start, cancellation and close ownership" as connection
  component "Native isolated execution\nactual selected ST controller\nconfigured plant or explicit prediction override" as isolated
  component "Runtime parameter/transfer transactions\ncomplete declared target binding\nobserved acknowledgement and recovery identities" as transactions
  component "Running ST controller and plant\nprimary journey: Control.PID\nexisting native simulated-plant adapters" as running
  component "Runtime experiment executor\ncontrol/experiment_handlers/executor.rs\nruns at the loop task's executions; observes each\nscan once; writes apply at the next task boundary" as runtime_executor
}

identify --> shared_ui
tune --> shared_ui
validate --> shared_ui
identify --> projection
tune --> projection
validate --> projection
identify --> tools
tune --> tools
tools --> projection
projection <--> panel : scoped messages and results
panel --> bindings : discover/select explicit target
panel --> flow : automatic operation
panel --> application : explicit Apply/Restore
panel --> engineer : edits and recovery
panel --> experiments : scoped review/start/abort
panel --> analysis : read-only calculations
experiments --> connection
experiments --> journals : recording and recovery identities
analysis <--> models : same selected model
analysis --> workers : existing bounded calculations
panel <--> persistence : restore/save study
panel <--> journals : ownership journals
shared_ui --> panel : native response context menu / recording export
panel --> shared_ui : current raw recording or immutable opened history
experiments --> projection : new operation resets live chart once
persistence --> projection : restore method, selected signals and retained trace
flow --> identification : live or recorded identification
flow --> engineer : Tune and Validate
identification <--> models : retained records and selected model
identification --> workers : fit one acquisition; provisional result
identification --> experiments : connected live acquisition
experiments --> running : bounded excitation + original-command restoration
running --> identification : native scan buffer + original recording
engineer <--> models : identical downstream model route
engineer --> automatic_criteria : fill missing test settings
automatic_criteria --> models : selected model and original recording
automatic_criteria --> persistence : values and automatic origin
engineer --> actions : one owner per requested action
actions --> tuning : candidate and shared test criteria
tuning --> workers : existing numerical methods
actions --> model_check : explicit Validate for provisional model
model_check --> identification : acquire independent record; no refit
model_check --> workers : predict and compare frozen model
model_check --> persistence : retain qualification and source records
actions --> campaign : require model pass; freeze controller scenarios
campaign --> prediction
campaign --> configured_validation
prediction --> isolated : explicit model override
configured_validation --> isolated : configured plant
application --> engineer : require current passed candidate
actions --> commissioning : exact reviewed target
commissioning --> transactions : adopt/restore complete binding
commissioning --> journals : durable recovery ownership
commissioning --> apply_obs : observe the applied response
isolated --> journals : retain operation identity and outcomes
transactions --> running : coherent parameter/state update
isolated --> running : prepare bytecode, then bounded actual-ST scans
identification --> connection
tuning --> connection : declared project tuning when needed
commissioning --> connection
isolated --> connection
transactions --> connection

setup_form <--> setup : draft / save or reason
setup --> bindings : compiled catalog
setup --> loop_files : new loop definitions
tuning --> prediction : Automatic response check; program-law candidate
panel --> readings : existing loop monitor snapshots
readings --> identify : initial response and current values

note bottom of flow
  Identification stops on its model for review.
  Tabs only navigate; Tune starts on request and stops at its candidate.\n  Validate starts the independent model check and controller campaign.
  Reset clears the working model, results and chart history.
  Live selected-signal observation continues after Reset/reopen.
  The chart grows from current plant readings during acquisition.
  Model comparisons retain the matching experiment inputs.
  Automatic continuation never dispatches Apply.
  All pages display the same host-owned study.
  A loop the engine serves runs Identify, Tune, Validate, Apply, Restore
  and Keep in trust-control-studio; the TypeScript session keeps parked
  loops and the features the engine does not serve yet (V7).
end note

note bottom of transactions
  A declared coherent multivariable adapter uses its complete binding.
  Separate PID instances are never updated by an invented sequential group write.
end note
identify --> reset : Reset
reset --> models : clear working model and recordings
reset --> engineer : clear dependent design evidence
reset --> panel : persist fresh draft
identification --> ident_campaign : one live campaign
ident_campaign --> experiments : start, hold, finish, restore
ident_campaign --> journals : journal before each dispatch
experiments --> runtime_executor : start, status, finish, abort
runtime_executor --> running : writes at the loop task's executions
apply_obs --> transactions : validated target change
apply_obs --> journals : observation identity and recording

actor "Engineer, script or CI" as cli_user
component "trust-lsp inline values\n(no Control Studio part)" as lsp_inline
cli_user --> rust_commands : trust-control-studio <verb>
panel --> engine_route : a loop the engine serves (V6)
engine_route --> rust_commands : serve: JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio, methods of §0.1a
engine_route --> projection : engine answers, updates and the opened study
lsp_inline --> rust_client : trust-runtime-client
rust_commands --> rust_control : decode, check, decide
rust_control --> rust_math : numbers in, typed results out
rust_commands --> rust_client : status, inspect, record, experiment
rust_commands <--> rust_studies : only writer
rust_commands <--> rust_journal : journal before dispatch; reattach (A8.5)
rust_client --> running : control.signals.inspect, control.recording.*, control.experiment.*,\ncontrol.transfer.*, control.parameters.*, control.simulation.run.*
component "trust-lsp command (spec 14 §7.8)\nheadless project commands: hmiBindings (setup catalog),\ncontrolKeepParameters, hmiEquipment (Keep's edits)" as lsp_command
rust_commands --> lsp_command : setup catalog; Keep's edit, written by the engine

note bottom of journals
  Closing the panel detaches this client only. A running identification
  experiment and its recording stay with the runtime; the campaign journal
  stays in workspace state; reopening reattaches and completes the campaign.
  A client that still owns its experiment aborts it only on an explicit
  Cancel or after a failure, through the restoration path.
  Closing during an Apply's observation detaches it the same way: the runtime
  keeps recording the response, and reopening reattaches at once, assesses it
  and reports the Apply's journalled transfers with the target change.
  An Apply interrupted before its observation began is recovered by reviewed
  recovery: the runtime recording is stopped, its samples are kept in the
  checkpoint and the runtime buffer is released.
end note

note bottom of persistence
  A legacy study copy in workspace state moves into the project on open.
  Removed from Control Studio: Manual Record, model-based validation
  (validation.ts), automatic tune (automaticTune.ts), and the automatic
  matched anti-windup comparison (no panel entry point).
  Protocol: docs/specs/control-studio-runtime-protocol.md;
  numerics: docs/specs/control-studio-numerics.md (replacing the satellite specs).
end note
@enduml
